cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use exga, please cite it as below."
title: "exga: risk-controlled data extraction from research-paper PDFs"
abstract: >-
  exga extracts user-defined fields from research-paper PDFs with a large language model,
  scores each value's confidence, and accepts a value only when its score clears a
  threshold certified on human-checked data, so that the error rate among accepted values
  of a field is at most a chosen alpha with probability at least 1 - delta. Other values
  are flagged for a person to check. A local web app covers the workflow from upload to
  export, and random audits keep the certification up to date.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Yaw Osei
    family-names: Adjei
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-25
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/yoadjei/exga"
keywords:
  - data extraction
  - systematic reviews
  - large language models
  - risk control
  - selective prediction
  - calibration
